.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_MD-MD5-SHA1 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_MD-MD5-SHA1
.Nd The MD5-SHA1 EVP_MD implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing MD5-SHA1 digests through the
.Sy EVP_MD
API.
.Pp
MD5-SHA1 is a rather special digest that's used with SSLv3.
.Ss Identity
This implementation is only available with the default provider, and is
identified with the name "MD5-SHA1".
.Ss Gettable Parameters
This implementation supports the common gettable parameters described in
.Xr EVP_MD-common 7 .
.Ss Settable Context Parameters
This implementation supports the following
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
entries, settable for an
.Sy EVP_MD_CTX
with
.Xr EVP_MD_CTX_set_params 3 :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqssl3-ms" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DIGEST_PARAM_SSL3_MS Ns ) <octet string>
This parameter is set by libssl in order to calculate a signature hash
for an SSLv3 CertificateVerify message as per RFC6101. It is only set
after all handshake messages have already been digested via
.Xr OP_digest_update 3
calls.
The parameter provides the master secret value to be added to the
digest.
The digest implementation should calculate the complete digest as per
RFC6101 section 5.6.8. The next call after setting this parameter should
be
.Xr OP_digest_final 3 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_MD_CTX_set_params 3 ,
.Xr provider-digest 7 ,
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER-default 7
